    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Fiery stones burst from the ground, filling a 20-foot-radius, 10-foot-tall Cylinder originating from a point on the ground you can see within range. Each creature in the Cylinder makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, it takes 1d12 Bludgeoning damage plus 3d8 Fire damage and is thrown up to the top of the Cylinder, from which it falls. On a success, it takes half as much damage only.</p><p>Smoldering stones make the ground in the Cylinder &amp;Reference[difficultterrain apply=false]{Difficult Terrain} until the end of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Using a Higher-Level Spell Slot.</strong> The Bludgeoning damage increases by 1d12 for each spell slot level above 4.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
